### characters/char-amina/state.jsonl
{"scene":"s-001","attribute":"location","value":"ship-simorgh deck","quote":"When the Simorgh swung at her moorings under the blistering sun of Port Rahim, Amina al-Sirafi stood at the rail as if the ship were a thing she could read with her hands. The deck smelled of hot tar and rope, of sweat and toasted cumin from the market stalls beyond the quay. Gulls thinned the air like thrown coins. She let the heat press at the back of her neck and listened to the harbor: men cursing, a bell that had lost its clapper, the slap of a loose sail against a yardarm."}
{"scene":"s-001","attribute":"holds","value":"dented brass compass","quote":"Her fingers found the dented brass of the compass she still carried—so familiar it had grooves where her thumb had worn them."}
{"scene":"s-001","attribute":"holds","value":"braided hair wrapped on wrist","quote":"A length of braided hair, knotted and wrapped until it looked more like rope than ornament, was looped around her wrist. She had braided it herself the week after the funeral and had not taken it off since."}
{"scene":"s-002","attribute":"location","value":"walking toward the quay","quote":"\"The city's heat pressed back up around her, and she walked toward the quay again with the knowledge that stories had become the sort of cargo that could sink you if you loaded them into your hull.\""}
{"scene":"s-002","attribute":"location","value":"loc-port-rahim","quote":"\"Amina left the Simorgh as if she were stepping from one weather into another. The heat of the deck eased into the market's reflux: a wall of smells and voices, hot tar and rope diluting into stall smoke and the sharp brightness of citrus. Gulls threaded the air like coins and the bell from the quay rang on without a clapper, a hollow sound that made the traders talk faster.\""}
{"scene":"s-002","attribute":"holds","value":"obj-compass","quote":"\"Her fingers found the outline of her compass beneath her coat and tightened, a private loop of muscle she did not bother to hide.\""}


